nodecode-showreel is a rewrite of Duffey234's Duffey234/hermes-showreel:

  https://github.com/Duffey234/hermes-showreel
  commit a8f404a0481408af8f56b514e47905dfd3565fa7
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Tim Duffey (Duffey234) (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the storyboard (a deterministic function of the session's own
history -- the ask, the tool calls and their results, the answer, the spend
-- with a failing step kept beside the step that fixed it, fitted to a hard
89 s and to the requested length), the two-pass secret scrub, the caption and
subtitle text, the aspect and resolution choices, the render folder, the
/showreel verbs and the model-facing render tool. The original recorded a
session through six observer hooks into a SQLite table of its own; Nodecode
already keeps that history as facts in its event log, so the rewrite reads it
there and writes nothing of its own but the video, its .srt and its poster.
The original drew frames with Pillow; the rewrite hands ffmpeg one drawtext
per beat over a colour source, so the only dependency is the ffmpeg the user
already has.

Left out: narration (the offline espeak-ng and piper voices, Hermes
text_to_speech, and the paid ElevenLabs path with its key, its per-beat
requests and its character plan) -- a cut here is captions only, so nothing
is synthesized and nothing leaves the machine. Also left out: the desktop
half (the Showreel page, the moment editor that drops beats and rewrites
captions, the inline player and the REC chip), the Hermes CLI subcommands,
the theme and font settings, image beats that read the pictures a tool
named, and the original's own SQLite store with its keep_sessions pruning.
